+From 3fca437b259a96058e552ab495c977a587f987ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
+Date: Wed, 6 May 2026 15:44:24 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Add core engine modules, open-fallback adjustment and
+ calibration tests
+MIME-Version: 1.0
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
+Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
+
+### Motivation
+
+- Provide a self-contained storage-layout engine implementing zone calculation, deterministic layouting, fit checking and a local open-fallback adjustment strategy for categories that can fall back to open storage.
+- Add calibration scenarios and automated checks to validate behavior for a base drawer and a forced open-fallback case.
+
+### Description
+
+- Introduce core types and libraries in `engine/types.ts` and `engine/libraries/defaultLibraries.ts` and wire a top-level API in `engine/index.ts` (`runUmestnoEngine`).
+- Implement input normalization/validation, volume→count conversion, storage requirement building and zone generation in `engine/input/*`, `engine/count/volumeToCount.ts`, `engine/requirements/*` and `engine/zones/*`.
+- Add deterministic layout plan builder and fit checker in `engine/layout/*` and `engine/fit/*`, plus an adjustment loop that computes and applies an `open` fallback per candidate in `engine/adjustment/*` using `calculateOpenCapacityInBox`.
+- Add calibration report builders, two calibration JSON reports and test runners in `engine/calibration/*` and `engine/test/*`, plus build config and scripts (`package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `.gitignore`).
+
+### Testing
+
+- Ran the build and calibration test script via `npm test` which runs `tsc` and `node dist/engine/test/runCalibration.js`.
+- The calibration test assertions in `engine/test/runCalibration.ts` passed and the script prints the expected success message (`ok 2 calibration case(s)`).
+- Manual generation helper `engine/test/printCalibrationCase.ts` can emit calibration JSON via the `calibration:json` and `calibration:json:forced-open` npm scripts.
